        "self_reported": {
          "assumptions": [
            "A rejected apply/retry attempt carries the invocation's cost block: the worker run behind a rejected tarball still spent it, and the rejected attempt is the one attempt that invocation writes.",
            "Cost is per run (the schema's 'the run's cost'), so a retry stamps only the spend of the run behind its own tarball; a harness passing a cumulative per-session total would double-count across attempts.",
            "Per-key validation follows ruling 4 literally: model_tier accepts any string (including empty) and models is recorded as handed, without enforcing the sorted-and-unique arithmetic that ruling 2 assigns to the harness."
          ],
          "judgment_calls": [
            "Clarification, apply --dry-run and the no-op unlock write no attempt, so a valid --cost-file is validated and logged as 'valid, not stamped' rather than refused or silently dropped.",
            "`bale unlock --integration --cost-file` refuses (a plain fail(); under --json the existing integration-json check fires first), the --reason contradiction's twin.",
            "build_telemetry_attempt overlays any caller's block on the all-null one, so every post-0.4.54 attempt carries six keys whatever subset it was handed; the old 'recorded verbatim' pin in test_telemetry_extensions moved with it.",
            "The schema also gains minimum 0 on tokens_in, tokens_out, usd and calls and minLength 1 on models items, so the record-side validator agrees with the writer-side reader.",
            "read_cost_file also refuses NaN/Infinity, a repeated key and non-UTF-8 bytes, and tolerates a UTF-8 byte-order mark; every problem is reported on one line with the path.",
            "The cost-file refusal is checked in apply after the --show-* inspection branch (which writes nothing), so inspection ignores the flag."
          ],
